# Core — the Fundamental Property and adequacy of `CDerivesP` under `PinLaw`  `[spec §28]`

GENERATED by `scripts/gen-pin.py` from `Core/Fundamental.lean` and
`scripts/pin/PinFundamental.tmpl.lean`. Edit the template, not this file.

* `fundamentalC_pin`: every `CDerivesP` derivation is sound, given `PinLaw`. Its induction is
  `Core.fundamentalC`'s, case for case, with one case per relaxed rule. R1's case is
  `PinLaw.stop`; R2's is `PinLaw.loop` at the rule's premises; `nilDead`'s is `semC_dead`.
* `adequacyC_pin`, `adequacyD_pin`, `adequacyD_pin_safe`: a closed `F 1` program of `CDerivesP`
  runs to `()` at the empty memory, on one run and on every run, and no run is stuck.
* `CDerivesP.ofC`: every `CDerives` derivation is a `CDerivesP` one. A program that uses no relaxed
  rule is a `CDerives` program, and `Core.fundamentalC` / `Core.adequacyD` cover it with no
  hypothesis.
-/

